                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1121 K 55/129: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Young</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-23T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>71. Repeat your No. 444, June 21, to Embassy London and Legation Christiania.</p>
                <p>Is it possible, in your opinion, that effective pressure for release of Americans
                    can be exercised by Baltic States in case they were asked to do so by this
                    Government?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
